  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1116 AM CDT Wed Oct 7 2026\n\nOur quiet weather will come to an end this weekend as Tropical\nStorm Isaias will eventually become Hurricane Isaias and make \nlandfall somewhere along the MS/AL/FL coast. The storm will \nweaken as it encounters land and progresses north towards Middle \nTN. 1-3\" of rain is possible with areas west of I-65 having a \nhigher likelihood of seeing the greatest amounts (50-60% chance of\n2\"+). 30-40 mph wind gusts are possible as well. The highest rain\nchances and strongest gusts will occur between Saturday afternoon\nand early Sunday with conditions improving through the day \nSunday. As of right now, significant impacts to Middle TN are not \nexpected. The severe threat remains low at this time but will be \nmonitored over the coming days, and any rain will be beneficial to\nongoing drought conditions.\n\nWe'll return to warm, dry weather at the start of next week with\nhighs in the 80s and comfortable humidity.",
